  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through nine innings until Devers walked it off in the tenth with one swing.",
    "what_this_means": "Webb grounded through six innings, giving the offense room to work. The bullpen held three scoreless from there. Smith struck out three in one, Foley bridged the gap, Miller and Kilian kept it even. Arraez went 3-for-5, staying above the chaos. But nothing stuck until the tenth: Devers had already driven in three runs by then, and now he delivered the final one. This is not a team that needs to lead early. They needed a closer with one swing, and they had him. One walk-off in ten innings is not a statement. It is survival, again.",
